## How Search Works in Slough

Slough's position between the M4 and Heathrow shapes who searches for Slough businesses.

Junctions 5, 6 and 7 of the M4 serve the town. Heathrow Airport is about 5 miles away. Its stations at Slough, Langley and Burnham have Elizabeth line services ([Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slough)).

Most Slough firms deal with three kinds of searcher.

**Residents** look for trades, clinics, solicitors, accountants and shops near home. Google's map results handle most of these searches. Your Google Business Profile, your reviews and a service page that names your part of Slough do most of the work.

**Businesses buying from businesses** judge suppliers on detailed service pages and evidence. A map listing is not enough for them. Procurement teams, facilities managers and engineers search for a capability or a supplier near their site.

**People passing through** come via Heathrow, the M4 and the rail links. Travellers, contractors and staff arrive from outside the borough. Hotels, food, parking, car services and venues need to show up in the searches people make before they arrive and on the day.

## Slough in Numbers

Slough is a borough of small businesses: nine in ten have fewer than 10 staff.

| Slough borough | Figure | Source |
|---|---:|---|
| VAT or PAYE registered businesses, 2026 | 6,780 | ONS UK Business Counts |
| Share with fewer than 10 staff | 90.2% | ONS UK Business Counts |
| Population, 2021 Census | 158,500 | ONS Census 2021 |
| Population change, 2011 to 2021 | +13.0% | ONS Census 2021 |
| Data centres on Slough Trading Estate, July 2025 | 31 | SEGRO |

The business counts are VAT or PAYE registered enterprises as of March 2026 ([ONS UK Business Counts](https://www.nomisweb.co.uk/datasets/idbrent)). The population figures come from the 2021 Census. Full links are in the sources list at the end of this page.

## Slough Trading Estate and B2B Firms

Slough Trading Estate firms usually win on detailed pages rather than on map results.

SEGRO has owned the estate since it opened in 1920. SEGRO describes it as a 420-acre site and the largest industrial estate in single ownership in Europe. SEGRO told Slough Borough Council on 11 July 2025 that the estate had 31 data centres and one more under construction ([Slough Borough Council](https://www.slough.gov.uk/downloads/file/4911/appendix-i-1-data-centre-development-segro)).

Buyers of estate firms search for a capability or a product. They often search from anywhere in the UK. A single "Services" page does not win those searches.

What usually works better:

- One page per capability with the specifications, sectors and standards a buyer checks
- Case studies and certifications on the page where buyers and Google can both see them
- A site structure that makes the link between your services clear
- Content that answers the questions buyers ask before they shortlist a supplier

I'll help you decide which searches are worth owning. I'll then build the pages that can earn them.

